@startuml per-store-idempotency
title US-11: Per-Store Idempotency - Same Key, Different Mechanism

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Position\nConsumer" as PosConsumer
participant "Correlation\nWorker" as CorrWorker
database "TimescaleDB\nposition_history" as TSDB
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
database "Neo4j\nentity graph" as Neo4j

note over PosConsumer
  Reads from adsb.raw / ais.raw.
  Writes to TimescaleDB and Redis.
end note

PosConsumer -> PosConsumer : derive idempotency key\n{entity_id}:{timestamp_ms}

PosConsumer -> TSDB : INSERT INTO position_history\n(entity_id, observed_at, timestamp_ms, lat, lon, geo_cell)\nON CONFLICT (entity_id, observed_at) DO NOTHING

note right of TSDB
  Duplicate row silently ignored.
  Conflict target is (entity_id, observed_at) —
  TimescaleDB requires the partition column in
  any unique constraint on a hypertable.
  observed_at = to_timestamp(timestamp_ms / 1000.0)
  is deterministically derived, so equivalent in practice.
end note

note over PosConsumer
  Redis HSET is NOT unconditionally idempotent.
  An older replayed event would overwrite a newer value.
  Timestamp guard required before every HSET.
end note

PosConsumer -> Redis : HGET entity:live:{entity_id} last_seen_ms
Redis --> PosConsumer : $stored_ms (or nil)

alt event.timestamp_ms > stored_ms (or nil)
  PosConsumer -> Redis : HSET entity:live:{entity_id}\nlat $lat lon $lon last_seen_ms $ts
  note right of Redis
    Write proceeds: event is newer than stored state.
    Conditional update prevents out-of-order replay
    from overwriting a more recent position.
  end note
else event.timestamp_ms <= stored_ms
  PosConsumer -> PosConsumer : skip Redis write\n(out-of-order or exact duplicate)
end

note over CorrWorker
  Reads from position.normalized.
  Writes PROXIMITY_EVENT edges to Neo4j.
  Idempotency key = {pair_key}:{episode_start_ms}
  (one edge per proximity episode, not per ping).
end note

CorrWorker -> CorrWorker : pair_key = min(a,b) + ':' + max(a,b)\nidempotency_key = pair_key + ':' + episode_start_ms

CorrWorker -> Neo4j : MERGE (a)-[e:PROXIMITY_EVENT {\n  idempotency_key: $key\n}]->(b)\nON CREATE SET e.episode_start_ms = $episode_start_ms,\n  e.distance_at_detection = $dist, e.lat = $lat, e.lon = $lon\nON MATCH SET e.last_seen_ms = $event_timestamp_ms

note right of Neo4j
  MERGE matches on idempotency_key.
  If edge exists — update last_seen_ms only.
  If edge absent — create it.
  Never produces duplicate edges per episode.
end note

@enduml
